WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.476 --> 00:00:01.309
- [Interviewer] Do you have a favorite

00:00:01.309 --> 00:00:02.265
character from the show?

00:00:02.265 --> 00:00:05.381
- I think the only answer to
that question is probably Tina.

00:00:05.381 --> 00:00:08.381
(ukulele strumming)

00:00:09.364 --> 00:00:11.323
My name is Andrew Rea, I
host a YouTube cooking show

00:00:11.323 --> 00:00:13.408
called Binging With Babish,
where I recreate the foods

00:00:13.408 --> 00:00:14.778
from movies and television.

00:00:14.778 --> 00:00:16.119
Binging With Babish, a lot of people think

00:00:16.119 --> 00:00:17.883
that my name is Oliver Babish, it's not.

00:00:17.883 --> 00:00:21.587
Oliver Babish is a character
from maybe three episodes

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:23.906
of The West Wing, a show that I love.

00:00:23.906 --> 00:00:25.746
I kinda started making the show just

00:00:25.746 --> 00:00:27.181
because I bought a camera and lights,

00:00:27.181 --> 00:00:29.934
and I wanted to practice
my food photography,

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:31.832
and I thought it would
be fun to make a burger

00:00:31.832 --> 00:00:32.835
from Parks and Rec.

00:00:32.835 --> 00:00:34.923
It just sort of grew and grew,

00:00:34.923 --> 00:00:37.016
and now it's my full-time job.

00:00:37.016 --> 00:00:40.504
So today we're making the
"Baby You Can Chive My Car"

00:00:40.504 --> 00:00:41.886
burger, from Bob's Burgers.

00:00:41.886 --> 00:00:44.882
This was one of the most
requested burgers on the show.

00:00:44.882 --> 00:00:48.700
And we're gonna start with a
step that most people forget.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:50.200
I'm gonna toast our buns.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.292
Be a good guy and toast
your buns for once.

00:00:52.292 --> 00:00:54.158
Droppin' in the buns.

00:00:54.158 --> 00:00:56.721
I've never seen Bob toast
his buns on the show,

00:00:56.721 --> 00:00:58.155
but again, this is a man who cares

00:00:58.155 --> 00:00:59.730
about the quality of his food.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:01.804
And anybody who knows burgers,
and Bob knows his burgers,

00:01:01.804 --> 00:01:04.692
knows that you gotta toast your bun.

00:01:04.692 --> 00:01:05.819
Come on, buddy.

00:01:05.819 --> 00:01:07.632
We have four toasted buns.

00:01:07.632 --> 00:01:09.170
Let us fry.

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:12.881
It's gonna get a little
smokey in here, folks.

00:01:12.881 --> 00:01:16.359
The price you pay for good food.

00:01:16.359 --> 00:01:18.477
I'm just hittin' these with just salt

00:01:18.477 --> 00:01:20.436
and freshly ground pepper.

00:01:20.436 --> 00:01:22.793
That is all that they need.

00:01:22.793 --> 00:01:24.430
That is all they want.

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:26.526
Two minutes, it'll slide right off.

00:01:26.526 --> 00:01:29.616
(playful claves with soft guitar picking)

00:01:29.616 --> 00:01:30.878
I started cooking when
I was like 10 or 11.

00:01:30.878 --> 00:01:32.421
My Mom taught me how to cook.

00:01:32.421 --> 00:01:33.716
She passed away when I was very young,

00:01:33.716 --> 00:01:36.309
so it's a nice way to just
sort of feel closer to her.

00:01:36.309 --> 00:01:38.459
Food's always been a huge part of me,

00:01:38.459 --> 00:01:39.951
and you know, so has film,

00:01:39.951 --> 00:01:43.080
so it's a really nice way
to combine those two things,

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:44.139
I'm very happy that I found a career

00:01:44.139 --> 00:01:45.618
that allows me to do that.

00:01:45.618 --> 00:01:47.143
Alright, I'm calling these done.

00:01:47.143 --> 00:01:50.185
No real cheese or
condiments on this burger,

00:01:50.185 --> 00:01:53.685
except for a healthy dollop of sour cream,

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:58.729
it goes with the chives.

00:01:58.729 --> 00:02:00.984
This wouldn't be the "Baby
You Can Chive My Car" burger

00:02:00.984 --> 00:02:05.179
without lots and lots
of chives, top it up.

00:02:05.179 --> 00:02:06.549
It wouldn't be the "Car" burger

00:02:06.549 --> 00:02:09.563
without our fried pickle wheels.

00:02:09.563 --> 00:02:11.617
I'm gettin' ready to
bread our pickles here.

00:02:11.617 --> 00:02:15.247
And I'm doing the classic
wet hand, dry hand method

00:02:15.247 --> 00:02:16.080
for breading these.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:17.813
That way you only have
one hand touching the egg,

00:02:17.813 --> 00:02:19.194
one hand touching the flour.

00:02:19.194 --> 00:02:20.361
We are frying.

00:02:21.323 --> 00:02:22.623
When you're laying things down in oil,

00:02:22.623 --> 00:02:24.481
lay them down away from you,

00:02:24.481 --> 00:02:27.170
flip it away from you, your hands

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:28.680
and your family and friends.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:31.993
There we go, we have
our fried pickle wheels.

00:02:31.993 --> 00:02:34.370
Going to impale them.

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:36.033
Just gonna slip 'em right in there.

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:39.802
That's, is the "Baby You
Can Chive My Car" burger.

00:02:39.802 --> 00:02:41.708
Vroom, vroom.

00:02:41.708 --> 00:02:43.562
I'm excited to see if people
like this as much as I do.

00:02:43.562 --> 00:02:44.587
- Ahhhh.

00:02:44.587 --> 00:02:45.420
- Oh my god.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:46.296
- It's so cute.

00:02:46.296 --> 00:02:47.129
- Ha!

00:02:47.129 --> 00:02:47.967
Cute little buggy.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:48.821
- Are those chicken nuggets?

00:02:48.821 --> 00:02:51.003
- No they're, they're fried pickles.

00:02:51.003 --> 00:02:53.393
It's like a car, it has little wheels.

00:02:53.393 --> 00:02:54.616
- Fucking love fried pickles.

00:02:54.616 --> 00:02:55.449
- I love fried pickles.

00:02:55.449 --> 00:02:57.088
- So we have to guess
the name of the burger.

00:02:57.088 --> 00:02:58.165
I'm not punn-ing.

00:02:58.165 --> 00:02:59.079
- I know the name of the burger.

00:02:59.079 --> 00:02:59.912
- You do?

00:02:59.912 --> 00:03:00.745
- Baby you can.

00:03:00.745 --> 00:03:01.692
- Chive my car.

00:03:01.692 --> 00:03:02.525
- Oh my god.

00:03:02.525 --> 00:03:03.980
- Cheers, oh my gosh.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:06.980
(light jazzy music)

00:03:07.938 --> 00:03:08.780
- Mmm.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:09.793
- Oh hell yeah.

00:03:09.793 --> 00:03:10.626
- Mm hmm.

00:03:10.626 --> 00:03:11.459
- Oh yeah.

00:03:11.459 --> 00:03:12.292
Mm hmm.

00:03:13.845 --> 00:03:14.678
- Fuck yeah.

00:03:14.678 --> 00:03:16.593
That is not a cartoon burger.

00:03:16.593 --> 00:03:18.232
That's like legit shit.

00:03:18.232 --> 00:03:19.065
- Love it.

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:21.361
- The pickle is definitely
a very important addition,

00:03:21.361 --> 00:03:23.234
like it adds a really nice like crunch.

00:03:23.234 --> 00:03:24.790
- I really love sour cream.

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:25.623
- Same.

00:03:25.623 --> 00:03:27.811
- And it's like the perfect
balance with the pickle.

00:03:27.811 --> 00:03:29.488
- Yeah, just up the chives I think.

00:03:29.488 --> 00:03:30.765
- We're chivey people.

00:03:30.765 --> 00:03:31.598
- Yeah, we're chivey people.

00:03:31.598 --> 00:03:33.639
Really amazing display by the way.

00:03:33.639 --> 00:03:35.374
- That was the coolest
burger I've ever seen.

00:03:35.374 --> 00:03:36.918
- These are the kinds of
burgers that they make

00:03:36.918 --> 00:03:38.320
at Bob's Burgers.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:39.703
- Why were they not more successful?

00:03:39.703 --> 00:03:41.655
- Like, I really want
like, Bob to serve me this.

00:03:41.655 --> 00:03:42.488
- Yeah.

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:43.423
- Because I think the whole part

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:44.454
of the Bob's Burgers experience is.

00:03:44.454 --> 00:03:45.605
- [Dark-Haired Girl] Is the characters.

00:03:45.605 --> 00:03:47.324
- [Green Sweater Guy]
It's the diner, it's the.

00:03:47.324 --> 00:03:48.485
- [Dark-Haired Girl] The family.

00:03:48.485 --> 00:03:49.528
- I feel like I just went to Bob's Bugers

00:03:49.528 --> 00:03:52.333
and I ordered a burger,
and that's like, my dream.

00:03:52.333 --> 00:03:54.244
- I just can't believe they
actually taste like that.

00:03:54.244 --> 00:03:56.562
I thought they were just
like crappy burgers.

00:03:56.562 --> 00:03:58.627
- Bring us more. (laughing)

00:03:58.627 --> 00:03:59.758
- Andrew, come back.

00:03:59.758 --> 00:04:00.608
- Or someone named Bob.

00:04:00.608 --> 00:04:02.203
- Someone named Bob.
- Bring a Bob.

00:04:02.203 --> 00:04:03.036
- Just a Bob, any Bob.

00:04:03.036 --> 00:04:04.085
- [Dark-Haired Girl] Just any kind of Bob,

00:04:04.085 --> 00:04:05.060
bring him over here and
make him make us a burger.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:07.705
- [Green Sweater Guy] Just a Bob, any Bob.

00:04:07.705 --> 00:04:09.496
(swishing wind)

00:04:09.496 --> 00:04:10.329
(squeaky hinge)

